{
 "_comment": "Storage categories (MAC-FIXES-FROM-WINDOWS §3.1, port of the Windows StorageClassifier). Patterns are lower-case folder paths: '/x' anchors at the disk root, '~/x' at any home (/Users/<name>), anything else matches the end of a path anywhere. Segments: '?' any one, 'x*' starts with, '*x' ends with, '*x*' contains. First matching rule wins, so specific rules come first. 'claim' takes the whole folder; 'area' sets the default class and keeps looking deeper. Advice: fine, review, warn (ask before adding to Cleanup), never (refuse). File rules (by name or extension) beat areas, never claims. A folder in Other or Documents & Desktop that holds a project marker (projectMarkers: .git, package.json, Cargo.toml…) becomes a Code & projects area.",
